# Trivia Platform QA Survey — Analysis & Recommendations

**26 responses** collected between May 13–17, 2026 across **CashRush** (17 responses, 65%) and **MindQuest** (8 responses, 31%). 1 response had no platform specified.

---

## Key Findings at a Glance

| Metric | Result | Severity |
|---|---|---|
| **Timer too fast** | **77% of users** said 10 seconds is too short | 🔴 Critical |
| **Question clarity** | 27% found questions confusing | 🟡 Moderate |
| **Factual accuracy** | 3.7/5 overall rating | 🟡 Moderate |
| **Difficulty level** | 81% said "Challenging but Fair" | 🟢 Good |
| **Typos/errors** | No concrete typos reported | 🟢 Good |

---

## 1. Timer Issue — 🔴 THE #1 PROBLEM

> [!CAUTION]
> **77% of all users (20/26) said the questions are too long for the 10-second timer.** This is the single most critical finding.

### Breakdown by Platform

| Platform | Too Fast | Just Right | Too Slow |
|---|---|---|---|
| **CashRush** | **15 / 17 (88%)** | 1 (6%) | 1 (6%) |
| **MindQuest** | 5 / 8 (63%) | 3 (37%) | 0 (0%) |

### Why This Matters
- CashRush questions average **130 characters** with **117/180 (65%)** exceeding 120 characters
- One user explicitly wrote: *"Over 7 out of 10 questions, I could not finish reading the question before the timer ends and there so many calculation questions that 10secs cannot be enough for"*
- Another said: *"No time. Before you try to understand the system picks an option automatically. I suggest the words should be few and little bit simpler"*

### Recommended Actions

| Priority | Action | Details |
|---|---|---|
| 🔴 P0 | **Shorten CashRush questions** | Target ≤ 80–90 characters (MindQuest's average). You already built a [batch question shortener tool](file:///c:/Users/admin/Projects/usertest/script.js) — use it on CashRush. |
| 🔴 P0 | **Increase timer to 15 seconds** | Even after shortening, bump the timer. 88% CashRush users ran out of time. |
| 🟡 P1 | **Remove calculation-heavy questions** | Users can't do mental math in 10–15s. Convert "calculate" questions into "which of these" recognition-style questions. |
| 🟡 P1 | **Add dynamic timer** | Consider making timer scale with question length (e.g., 10s base + 1s per 20 chars over 80). |

---

## 2. Question Clarity — 🟡 NEEDS WORK

### Overall Clarity Distribution

| Rating | Count | % |
|---|---|---|
| Very Clear | 4 | 15% |
| Mostly Clear | 15 | 58% |
| Somewhat Confusing | 6 | 23% |
| Very Confusing | 1 | 4% |

### Breakdown by Platform

| Rating | CashRush | MindQuest |
|---|---|---|
| Very Clear | 1 (6%) | 3 (37%) |
| Mostly Clear | 11 (65%) | 3 (37%) |
| Somewhat Confusing | 4 (24%) | 2 (25%) |
| Very Confusing | 1 (6%) | 0 (0%) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **CashRush has a clarity problem.** Only 6% rated it "Very Clear" versus 37% for MindQuest. Combined, 30% of CashRush users found questions somewhat-to-very confusing.

### Recommended Actions

| Priority | Action | Details |
|---|---|---|
| 🔴 P0 | **Simplify CashRush question language** | Reduce jargon. Replace technical financial terms with plain-English equivalents where possible. |
| 🟡 P1 | **Review "Somewhat Confusing" question categories** | Focus on the categories that produced the most confusion — likely Investment Basics and Compound Finance. |
| 🟡 P1 | **Add context hints for technical terms** | Consider a brief tooltip or parenthetical definition for terms like "portfolio diversification" or "compound interest". |

---

## 3. Factual Accuracy — 🟡 DECENT BUT ROOM TO IMPROVE

### Rating Distribution (1–5 scale)

| Rating | CashRush | MindQuest |
|---|---|---|
| ⭐ 1 | 1 | 0 |
| ⭐ 2 | 2 | 0 |
| ⭐ 3 | 3 | 3 |
| ⭐ 4 | 5 | 3 |
| ⭐ 5 | 6 | 2 |
| **Average** | **3.8 / 5** | **3.9 / 5** |

> [!NOTE]
> Accuracy is acceptable but not stellar. 3 CashRush users rated accuracy at 1 or 2, suggesting some questions may have incorrect answers or misleading distractors.

### Recommended Actions

| Priority | Action | Details |
|---|---|---|
| 🟡 P1 | **Audit low-confidence questions** | Review questions where users scored ≤ 2 on accuracy. Cross-verify correct answers against authoritative sources. |
| 🟡 P1 | **Improve distractor quality** | Ensure incorrect answers are plausible but clearly wrong — not ambiguous or "technically also correct". |

---

## 4. Difficulty — 🟢 ON TARGET

| Rating | Count | % |
|---|---|---|
| Too Easy | 1 | 4% |
| Challenging but Fair | 21 | 81% |
| Too Hard/Technical | 4 | 15% |

> [!TIP]
> 81% "Challenging but Fair" is an excellent result — the difficulty calibration is well-tuned. The 4 "Too Hard" responses are all from users who also cited timer/clarity issues, suggesting the perceived difficulty stems from **presentation**, not content.

---

## 5. Typos & Errors — 🟢 NO ISSUES FOUND

No concrete typos or incorrect answers were reported. The 2 "meaningful" feedback entries focused on question length and timer complaints, not factual errors.

---

## Summary: Prioritized Action Plan

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["🔴 P0: Shorten CashRush Questions"] --> B["Target ≤ 80-90 chars avg"]
    A --> C["Remove/convert calculation questions"]
    D["🔴 P0: Increase Timer"] --> E["10s → 15s minimum"]
    D --> F["Consider dynamic timer by length"]
    G["🟡 P1: Improve CashRush Clarity"] --> H["Simplify jargon"]
    G --> I["Add context for technical terms"]
    J["🟡 P1: Audit Accuracy"] --> K["Review low-rated questions"]
    J --> L["Improve distractor quality"]
```

| # | Priority | Task | Effort |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 🔴 P0 | **Shorten CashRush question text** to ≤ 90 chars average | Medium — use your batch shortener tool |
| 2 | 🔴 P0 | **Increase timer from 10s to 15s** in `script.js` | Trivial — change `timeLeft = 10` to `15` |
| 3 | 🔴 P0 | **Remove/rewrite calculation-heavy questions** that require mental math | Medium |
| 4 | 🟡 P1 | **Simplify CashRush language** — reduce jargon, use plain English | Medium |
| 5 | 🟡 P1 | **Audit accuracy** — verify correct answers for any flagged questions | Low |
| 6 | 🟢 P2 | **Consider dynamic timer** scaling with question length | Low |
| 7 | 🟢 P2 | **MindQuest is in good shape** — minor clarity tweaks only | Low |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Bottom line: The questions themselves are well-calibrated for difficulty (81% say "Challenging but Fair") — the problem is that they're too long to read in 10 seconds, especially CashRush.** The fix is a combination of shortening questions and extending the timer.
